## 5. Algorithmic Breakdown: Manual DSA Implementations

Every data structure and algorithm in DeptFlow V2 is written **from scratch without STL containers** (`std::vector`, `std::map`, `std::queue`, `std::sort` are absent):

| Data Structure / Algorithm       | Source File        | Implementation Details                                                           | Practical Role                                                                                                                                  |                      Time Complexity                      |         Space Complexity         |
| :------------------------------- | :----------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-------------------------------------------------------: | :------------------------------: |
| **Max-Heap (Priority Queue)**    | `backend/dsa.h`    | Array-based binary heap with `siftUp()` and `siftDown()` methods.                | Prioritizes sessions with high conflict probability: Outside Practicals (110) > Dept Practicals (100) > Outside Theory (55) > Dept Theory (30). | Push: $\mathcal{O}(\log N)$<br>Pop: $\mathcal{O}(\log N)$ |         $\mathcal{O}(N)$         |
| **Adjacency Matrix Graph + BFS** | `backend/dsa.h`    | 2D matrix `adj[MAX_DIVS][MAX_DIVS]` with manual FIFO queue.                      | Traverses division network to distinguish **direct dependencies** (shared faculty edge) from **indirect transitive ripple effects**.            |                  BFS: $\mathcal{O}(V^2)$                  |        $\mathcal{O}(V^2)$        |
| **Separate Chaining Hash Table** | `backend/dsa.h`    | 17-bucket array with polynomial rolling hash ($h = (h \cdot 31 + c) \pmod{17}$). | Provides constant-time lookup, insertion, and deletion of faculty records by alphanumeric ID.                                                   |   Average: $\mathcal{O}(1)$<br>Worst: $\mathcal{O}(N)$    |       $\mathcal{O}(B + N)$       |
| **Singly Linked List**           | `backend/models.h` | Dynamic pointer chain `CommitNode*` attached to each visiting faculty.           | Stores external home-department blocks (day, slot) that the scheduler must avoid.                                                               |   Search: $\mathcal{O}(K)$<br>Insert: $\mathcal{O}(1)$    |         $\mathcal{O}(K)$         |
| **Undo Stack**                   | `backend/dsa.h`    | LIFO static array with top pointer.                                              | Enables atomic rollback of manual timetable edits without full regeneration.                                                                    |      Push: $\mathcal{O}(1)$<br>Pop: $\mathcal{O}(1)$      |         $\mathcal{O}(S)$         |
| **Insertion Sort**               | `backend/dsa.h`    | In-place comparison sort.                                                        | Chronologically sorts session records by day and time slot before sending to UI.                                                                |    Worst: $\mathcal{O}(N^2)$<br>Best: $\mathcal{O}(N)$    |         $\mathcal{O}(1)$         |
| **Binary Search**                | `backend/dsa.h`    | Divide-and-conquer search on sorted subject list.                                | Rapid lookup of subject specifications by code.                                                                                                 |                   $\mathcal{O}(\log M)$                   |         $\mathcal{O}(1)$         |
| **3D Occupancy Grid**            | `backend/models.h` | `grid[MAX_DIVS][MAX_DAYS][MAX_SLOTS]`                                            | Constant-time access to any division's timetable cell.                                                                                          |                 Access: $\mathcal{O}(1)$                  | $\mathcal{O}(D \cdot W \cdot S)$ |

