## 6. Single Source of Truth Timing Engine

DeptFlow V2 computes all schedule grids dynamically from the department configuration:

$$\text{numSlots} = \left\lfloor \frac{\text{parseMinutes}(\text{endTime}) - \text{parseMinutes}(\text{startTime})}{\text{interval}} \right\rfloor$$

When the department time parameters (`startTime`, `endTime`, `interval`) or working days change:

1. `Department::recalculateSlots()` computes the new slot boundaries (e.g. `09:00-10:00`, `10:00-11:00`).
2. Existing timetable grids adapt their time axes dynamically.
3. Multi-slot practical sessions dynamically scale their required slot span based on the configured interval ($\text{pracDurSlots} = \max(1, \text{practicalDuration} / \text{interval})$).
